1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,156
[March 2026]

2
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,064
Ugh...

3
00:00:56,064 --> 00:00:58,016
[Horai Consulting]

4
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:59,712
Huh? You're quitting?

5
00:00:59,712 --> 00:01:02,048
Yes, I achieved my whimsical gap FIRE.

6
00:01:02,048 --> 00:01:04,192
Huh? Whimsical what? What's that?

7
00:01:04,192 --> 00:01:06,432
Um, first, do you know what FIRE is?

8
00:01:06,432 --> 00:01:07,552
As in burning?

9
00:01:07,552 --> 00:01:09,624
[FIRE]
Not that, but through things like

10
00:01:09,624 --> 00:01:10,624
[Financial Independence Retire Early]
investments and asset management,

11
00:01:10,624 --> 00:01:12,384
I can cover my living expenses now.

12
00:01:12,384 --> 00:01:14,208
[Consultant, Anna Kusakabe]
And then I can just quit my job. That's it.

13
00:01:14,208 --> 00:01:15,840
[Zapaan Sales Clerk]
Oh, my! So that means you're now one of

14
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,151
[Kiko Kominami]
those people who can live without working?

15
00:01:18,151 --> 00:01:21,696
No, in my case, I just can
barely cover my living expenses.

16
00:01:21,696 --> 00:01:23,840
[Come work at Zapaan!]
Well, I can live by whim to some extent.

17
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,632
But when I want to have fun or splurge,

18
00:01:25,632 --> 00:01:27,520
I still have to pick up
some odd jobs. Like that.

19
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,896
That's why I call it whimsical gap FIRE.

20
00:01:28,896 --> 00:01:31,360
So would you call that wonderful?

21
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:33,536
Yes, it's wonderful. It's my dream.

22
00:01:33,536 --> 00:01:34,856
[Consultant]
Doing what I love when I want,

23
00:01:34,856 --> 00:01:36,384
[Ren Fuchinobe]
and doing odd jobs I love in my spare time.

24
00:01:36,384 --> 00:01:37,952
So whimsical!

25
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:39,456
I'm against it.

26
00:01:39,456 --> 00:01:42,176
Ms. Kusakabe is our top ace.

27
00:01:42,176 --> 00:01:45,920
All her consulting clients' results
have shot straight up,

28
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,360
especially this one.

29
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,960
[Case Introduction]
The Kitchen Sakoda project.

30
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:51,520
In just two years,
turning a local Western restaurant

31
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,728
into a brand capable of expanding worldwide.

32
00:01:53,728 --> 00:01:55,584
Truly the stuff of legend.

33
00:01:55,584 --> 00:01:57,408
And yet this is your last project?

34
00:01:57,408 --> 00:01:59,008
And you're quitting the company,
quitting consulting?

35
00:01:59,008 --> 00:02:00,352
Yes, thank you.

36
00:02:00,352 --> 00:02:05,396
But, you know, all that stuff about
the past, this and that, it's all...

37
00:02:07,872 --> 00:02:10,304
Zapaan!

38
00:02:10,304 --> 00:02:12,480
It all washed away, didn't it?

39
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:19,980
So I'm going to fully enjoy
my whimsical gap FIRE!

40
00:02:21,664 --> 00:02:24,404
So cute!

41
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,608
I wonder if you'll get
the one you're targeting?

42
00:02:32,608 --> 00:02:36,308
This moment is so thrilling, isn't it?

43
00:02:37,632 --> 00:02:41,108
Go, go!

44
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,556
Yay!

45
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:49,780
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

46
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:56,480
Whimsical, whimsical.

47
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,480
Welcome!

48
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:59,200
So good!

49
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:05,792
Whimsical, whimsical, whimsical...

50
00:03:05,792 --> 00:03:07,290
Whimsical.

51
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:10,850
<i>♪ Wanting to cry, wanting to laugh ♪</i>

52
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:12,800
<i>♪ My true self ♪</i>

53
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,224
<i>♪ Holding back, not laughing the whole time ♪</i>

54
00:03:16,224 --> 00:03:19,744
<i>♪ I can't say painful things ♪</i>

55
00:03:19,744 --> 00:03:22,334
<i>♪ But I'm right here ♪</i>

56
00:03:22,334 --> 00:03:25,760
<i>♪ Wanting to cry, wanting to laugh ♪</i>

57
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,680
<i>♪ My true self ♪</i>

58
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:31,712
[Whimsically traversing Japan,
Hokkaido to Okinawa! Send support!]

59
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:37,152
<i>♪ You live your life for yourself ♪</i>

60
00:03:37,152 --> 00:03:42,444
This spring, that Cynical Molco is going to
be all cynical on screens nationwide!

61
00:03:43,552 --> 00:03:46,272
Cynical Molco: The Movie!

62
00:03:46,272 --> 00:03:50,124
Super love, that kind of thing. Hmph.

63
00:03:51,456 --> 00:03:54,560
Is this what it was like, everyone?

64
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,248
So cute!

65
00:03:57,248 --> 00:03:59,552
Who wants to see it soon?

66
00:03:59,552 --> 00:04:02,208
Me!

67
00:04:02,208 --> 00:04:06,016
Molco, how did you feel
listening to everyone's wishes?

68
00:04:06,016 --> 00:04:08,404
That kind of thing. Hmph.

69
00:04:14,176 --> 00:04:16,000
Great work!

70
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Hot, hot, hot!
Summer, it's summer only for me!

71
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:25,440
Cynical Molco: The Movie,
now issuing numbered tickets!

72
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,500
Thank you very much.

73
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:32,192
Serving somen here?
You really know your stuff, Mugi.

74
00:04:32,192 --> 00:04:36,564
Well, this is hiyamugi.
And since I'm Mugi, here you go.

75
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,750
Kind of like love, isn't it?

76
00:04:41,952 --> 00:04:43,808
No, no way.

77
00:04:43,808 --> 00:04:46,400
N-N-No. That's cute.

78
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,352
- Love.
- That's so cute.

79
00:04:48,352 --> 00:04:49,440
Geez.

80
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,924
- Hey! Come on! Let's eat!
- Hmm.

81
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,912
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

82
00:04:54,912 --> 00:04:57,696
Huh? What? You bought more?

83
00:04:57,696 --> 00:04:59,840
Ah, Shiro.

84
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:02,821
I did FIRE, and then I thought
I'd go all out doing what I love,

85
00:05:02,821 --> 00:05:05,024
so I bought various things, but...

86
00:05:05,024 --> 00:05:07,680
[Anna's boyfriend, Mugi Koitabashi]
You haven't found something you love yet?

87
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,960
That's right.

88
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:12,959
Ever since I was born, I've lived
a life without love or obsession.

89
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:14,656
And unfortunately, this time too,
I also didn't get into it.

90
00:05:14,656 --> 00:05:18,752
But the part-time job you did today
was full of love, wasn't it?

91
00:05:18,752 --> 00:05:19,904
That's right.

92
00:05:19,904 --> 00:05:23,488
Everyone was going on about
how cute Cynical Molco is.

93
00:05:23,488 --> 00:05:27,968
I've had a life where I never
got into so-called characters,

94
00:05:27,968 --> 00:05:30,240
so I don't get cute.

95
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,320
Well, I get it logically.

96
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:38,304
But not that heart-throbbing,
"I love it!" kind of sensory cute.

97
00:05:38,304 --> 00:05:39,968
An encounter with the unknown.

98
00:05:39,968 --> 00:05:45,396
Hmm. Well, when it comes to cute,
for example, something like this as well.

99
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:53,248
Well, really, it's fine even if you
don't understand love or cuteness.

100
00:05:53,248 --> 00:05:55,644
That's right.

101
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:01,020
- See you.
- Okay, see you.

102
00:06:09,664 --> 00:06:12,864
My name is Kusakabe, and I applied
through Suppori Gap Part-time Jobs.

103
00:06:12,864 --> 00:06:15,808
[Seo Design]

104
00:06:15,808 --> 00:06:16,864
Um, today...

105
00:06:16,864 --> 00:06:20,960
I was thinking of digitizing receipts
and other money-related stuff.

106
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,584
But then one thing led to another.

107
00:06:23,584 --> 00:06:27,476
In the three years since I started here?
Stuff has piled up like crazy.

108
00:06:28,128 --> 00:06:29,716
I see.

109
00:06:35,648 --> 00:06:37,376
No, I mean, I'll do my best.

110
00:06:37,376 --> 00:06:42,228
- I'll be in your care today...
- Alright.

111
00:06:43,232 --> 00:06:45,076
Excuse me.

112
00:06:56,512 --> 00:06:58,496
I've already organized all this,
so just wrap it up quickly.

113
00:06:58,496 --> 00:07:00,308
- Oh, okay.
- Alright.

114
00:07:09,856 --> 00:07:11,936
- Hmm?
- Oh, sorry.

115
00:07:11,936 --> 00:07:17,748
I heard this was a design office, but I was
wondering if you specialize in characters?

116
00:07:18,464 --> 00:07:19,710
[Character Designer, Mizuki Seo]

117
00:07:19,710 --> 00:07:21,460
Do you really need that information?

118
00:07:22,784 --> 00:07:24,372
- No.
- Right, of course not.

119
00:07:25,248 --> 00:07:29,588
Right, right, right, right.

120
00:07:40,768 --> 00:07:46,804
Whimsical, whimsical, whimsical, whim...

121
00:07:49,216 --> 00:07:52,028
Takai Create.

122
00:07:55,648 --> 00:07:58,060
Excuse me.

123
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,924
Excuse me.

124
00:08:00,832 --> 00:08:03,328
Excuse me!

125
00:08:03,328 --> 00:08:05,536
- Why are you shouting all of a sudden?
- Sorry.

126
00:08:05,536 --> 00:08:08,732
There's something I'd like to
talk to you about.

127
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:11,744
Yes?

128
00:08:11,744 --> 00:08:15,168
Excuse me, I'm Takai from Takai Create.

129
00:08:15,168 --> 00:08:16,948
Hello.

130
00:08:18,528 --> 00:08:21,504
[Company Character Material]
Yes, yes, exactly like this.

131
00:08:21,504 --> 00:08:22,528
Let's go with this.

132
00:08:22,528 --> 00:08:23,910
[Takai Create, Shinpei Takai]

133
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:27,028
All right, let's see.

134
00:08:27,744 --> 00:08:29,568
How about 8,000 yen?

135
00:08:29,568 --> 00:08:33,440
8,000... That's quite a lot.

136
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:37,430
All right, now the next one. Let's see.

137
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:39,168
There's a company called Marui Bedding.

138
00:08:39,168 --> 00:08:40,576
- They want an original character
- Um...

139
00:08:40,576 --> 00:08:42,780
- for their storefront...
- Excuse me.

140
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:45,376
What, eavesdropping?

141
00:08:45,376 --> 00:08:48,380
No, I mean...

142
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:51,744
- That's too cheap.
- Huh?

143
00:08:51,744 --> 00:08:53,856
Of course, the fees for
this kind of industry,

144
00:08:53,856 --> 00:08:56,640
I know they vary widely,
but from a quick check,

145
00:08:56,640 --> 00:09:00,000
this is a third of
the market rate, or rather.

146
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,844
A third?

147
00:09:02,848 --> 00:09:05,056
No matter how you look at it,

148
00:09:05,056 --> 00:09:07,220
- that's just not right.
- But

149
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:13,280
paying the market rate to a no-name designer
with no standout experience...

150
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:16,416
That's a bit, you know.

151
00:09:16,416 --> 00:09:17,510
Hmm?

152
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:22,496
Anyway, I'm actually
trying to support you here.

153
00:09:22,496 --> 00:09:27,488
Even if the pay is low, I want you to build
your career with us and seize opportunities!

154
00:09:27,488 --> 00:09:30,580
I don't think that's support.

155
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,584
It's just coated with
the nice-sounding word "support".

156
00:09:35,584 --> 00:09:36,992
Wait, what are you saying?

157
00:09:36,992 --> 00:09:41,120
But actually, there are people
who have produced results from that.

158
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:44,320
Don't try to cover up
your crimes with results!

159
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,984
Crimes, you say?

160
00:09:45,984 --> 00:09:49,632
First, have you even issued
an order specifying the amount?

161
00:09:49,632 --> 00:09:50,944
Since the new freelance law,

162
00:09:50,944 --> 00:09:54,944
starting work without stating
the compensation for no valid reason,

163
00:09:54,944 --> 00:09:58,144
and just proceeding vaguely,
could potentially be illegal!

164
00:09:58,144 --> 00:10:01,600
But even with all that said, Mr. Seo,
you still need a job, right?

165
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:04,864
I'm saying that you should admit
what you're doing first!

166
00:10:04,864 --> 00:10:08,660
The fact that you're exploiting
someone's liking for you,

167
00:10:11,392 --> 00:10:14,484
misusing it,

168
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,332
is a crime!

169
00:10:24,512 --> 00:10:26,452
Understood.

170
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,732
Excuse me.

171
00:10:36,448 --> 00:10:39,028
- Hmm?
- Hmm?

172
00:10:40,096 --> 00:10:43,200
Um, no, that's not it!
I just want a price that's within reason.

173
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:47,828
I see. But we'll probably
never meet again, right?

174
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:56,384
I'm sorry, I messed up.

175
00:10:56,384 --> 00:10:58,400
Yeah, you messed up all right!
You messed up big time!

176
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,776
- Um...
- That person is my biggest client,

177
00:10:59,776 --> 00:11:00,960
and if they're gone...

178
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,656
So, uh, when the blood rushes to my head,

179
00:11:02,656 --> 00:11:03,968
I kind of turn into that guy
from The Shining...

180
00:11:03,968 --> 00:11:05,024
Um, I'll go apologize.

181
00:11:05,024 --> 00:11:06,024
I'll do something like bowing down

182
00:11:06,024 --> 00:11:07,520
- and getting work again...
- It's fine.

183
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:09,632
But...

184
00:11:09,632 --> 00:11:11,188
Go home.

185
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:14,708
- I'll transfer the pay.
- No! The money...

186
00:11:15,904 --> 00:11:19,412
Then please let me help with the management.

187
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:23,290
Let me make up for the losses
caused by this incident

188
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:24,820
by helping with the management.

189
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:26,686
For free, of course.

190
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:28,192
No, it's fine.

191
00:11:28,192 --> 00:11:29,280
Um, no, that's not it.

192
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:34,368
I used to work at a consulting company,
so please don't be suspicious about anything.

193
00:11:34,368 --> 00:11:35,808
No, it's fine, really.

194
00:11:35,808 --> 00:11:38,912
Huh? Why? Because I'm
offering to do it for free?

195
00:11:38,912 --> 00:11:42,688
But what I'm offering is a non-suspicious
free service, a harmless freebie.

196
00:11:42,688 --> 00:11:45,024
That's not it. Why are you doing this?

197
00:11:45,024 --> 00:11:47,904
Please, let me do it.

198
00:11:47,904 --> 00:11:49,120
Otherwise, I...

199
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:53,524
At this rate... At this rate,
I'll once again...

200
00:11:56,064 --> 00:11:58,388
Please let me pay you 10,000 yen.

201
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:02,496
Let me help you for 10,000 yen.

202
00:12:02,496 --> 00:12:04,192
What do you mean, pay?

203
00:12:04,192 --> 00:12:08,160
Then 20,000?

204
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:12,992
30,000? 35,000? 40,000?

205
00:12:12,992 --> 00:12:16,864
- Oh! The Shining!
- 45,000?

206
00:12:16,864 --> 00:12:19,508
The Shining!

207
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:33,632
<i>♪ The client's work ♪</i>

208
00:12:33,632 --> 00:12:38,368
<i>♪ Meddling and erasing everything ♪</i>

209
00:12:38,368 --> 00:12:42,688
<i>♪ Cuteness I don't understand at all ♪</i>

210
00:12:42,688 --> 00:12:48,352
<i>♪ Declaring I'd help with management ♪</i>

211
00:12:48,352 --> 00:12:56,352
<i>♪ Because I'm a girl who messes up ♪</i>

212
00:12:57,312 --> 00:13:06,312
<i>♪ So I'm a girl who messes up ♪</i>

213
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,880
[Episode 1]

214
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,792
In helping with the management,

215
00:13:25,792 --> 00:13:30,016
I'd like to share the future vision of
Seo Design that you envision.

216
00:13:30,016 --> 00:13:31,072
And on that basis,

217
00:13:31,072 --> 00:13:33,600
- as we move toward solving the issues...
- A big hit!

218
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,624
A big hit?

219
00:13:34,624 --> 00:13:37,632
No, I mean I want to create
a character that's a big hit.

220
00:13:37,632 --> 00:13:43,104
So first, can you think of a concept?

221
00:13:43,104 --> 00:13:44,352
A concept.

222
00:13:44,352 --> 00:13:46,816
A concept that will be a big hit.

223
00:13:46,816 --> 00:13:49,312
Then I'll draw the character
according to that,

224
00:13:49,312 --> 00:13:51,264
which will guarantee a big hit.

225
00:13:51,264 --> 00:13:55,552
A concept that will be a big hit.

226
00:13:55,552 --> 00:13:57,088
Hey, you can do that, right?

227
00:13:57,088 --> 00:14:00,160
Because you'll make up for
what you messed up, right?

228
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,184
You want to make up for it, right?

229
00:14:01,184 --> 00:14:06,036
By the way... By the way,
the scale of that hit is...

230
00:14:07,264 --> 00:14:11,232
This guy. I want to surpass
this guy, at the very least.

231
00:14:11,232 --> 00:14:12,300
[Cynical Molco]
<i>Hmph.</i>

232
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:15,552
- Cynical Molco?
- That's right.

233
00:14:15,552 --> 00:14:18,144
- Well, it...
- You can do it, right?

234
00:14:18,144 --> 00:14:20,852
- Thank you for your hard work.
- Thank you for your hard work!

235
00:14:23,072 --> 00:14:24,640
Zapaan!

236
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:27,808
Saying you'll make up for the losses
by creating a big hit?

237
00:14:27,808 --> 00:14:33,984
Isn't that a bit much? Ugh, just forget it.

238
00:14:33,984 --> 00:14:37,248
But it was me who asked him to let me do it.

239
00:14:37,248 --> 00:14:41,236
But Cynical Molco is so popular.

240
00:14:43,648 --> 00:14:44,773
Huh?

241
00:14:44,773 --> 00:14:47,482
Isn't Molco from the same company
that made Hello Kitty?

242
00:14:47,482 --> 00:14:50,148
No, Molco was made by
a design company called Merry.

243
00:14:50,148 --> 00:14:53,232
Merry... I've never heard of it.

244
00:14:53,232 --> 00:14:55,023
Berry is also from Merry.

245
00:14:55,023 --> 00:14:57,273
Hey! You mean Very Good Berry?

246
00:14:57,273 --> 00:15:00,064
Hey, look, look.

247
00:15:00,064 --> 00:15:05,240
Look! See? I've loved it for a long time.

248
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:09,232
But kids these days might not know.

249
00:15:09,232 --> 00:15:10,773
That's true.

250
00:15:10,773 --> 00:15:13,607
Merry is actually a pretty veteran brand.

251
00:15:13,607 --> 00:15:15,307
They're known for the success of Berry,

252
00:15:15,307 --> 00:15:17,648
which launched around
the same time as Hello Kitty.

253
00:15:17,648 --> 00:15:20,565
But after that, they couldn't
raise their profile and stagnated.

254
00:15:20,565 --> 00:15:24,232
But then, about five years ago,
this person came from outside.

255
00:15:24,232 --> 00:15:26,315
[Character Business Revolution]
Giant salamander?

256
00:15:26,315 --> 00:15:28,107
Takumi Omishima.

257
00:15:28,107 --> 00:15:29,536
Once he became president,

258
00:15:29,536 --> 00:15:32,864
Merry underwent reform, reform,
and mega-reform!

259
00:15:32,864 --> 00:15:34,273
And then three years ago,

260
00:15:34,273 --> 00:15:37,273
a cute guinea pig
that spouted cynical remarks,

261
00:15:37,273 --> 00:15:40,607
Cynical Molco, became a huge hit,
and their earnings made a V-shaped recovery.

262
00:15:40,607 --> 00:15:42,148
Molco's signature line,

263
00:15:42,148 --> 00:15:43,815
- That kind of thing. Hmph.
- "That kind of thing. Hmph,"

264
00:15:43,815 --> 00:15:46,190
went viral on social media like crazy.

265
00:15:46,190 --> 00:15:48,773
I use that same expression too.

266
00:15:48,773 --> 00:15:52,857
Breakfast smoothies,
that kind of thing. Hmph.

267
00:15:53,898 --> 00:16:00,276
Anyway, trying to surpass it
could be extremely reckless.

268
00:16:01,344 --> 00:16:06,560
[Asia Sunshine Market]

269
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:09,232
All the tests and everything
tomorrow are really a drag.

270
00:16:09,232 --> 00:16:11,232
Yumi is absent from school
because of a fandom activity.

271
00:16:11,232 --> 00:16:13,216
Really? That level of love is

272
00:16:13,216 --> 00:16:16,440
- that kind of thing. Hmph.
- That kind of thing. Hmph.

273
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,624
- Molco!
- Molco!

274
00:16:18,624 --> 00:16:22,732
It really is that kind of thing. Hmph.

275
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:25,190
Ah, that looks yummy.
Which one should I choose?

276
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:26,464
[Seo Design]
Modern society,

277
00:16:26,464 --> 00:16:28,190
while making it easier to connect,

278
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:31,148
also has the contradiction of
making it easier to feel lonely.

279
00:16:31,148 --> 00:16:34,523
That's exactly why a character
that connects people...

280
00:16:34,523 --> 00:16:37,696
No, no, no. That's completely wrong.

281
00:16:37,696 --> 00:16:39,357
Well, um...

282
00:16:39,357 --> 00:16:45,065
Just as I thought,
free stuff is cheap and nasty.

283
00:16:45,065 --> 00:16:48,732
Yeah, it's that saying.
You get what you pay for.

284
00:16:49,376 --> 00:16:51,898
I really want to
get going on drawing quickly.

285
00:16:51,898 --> 00:16:55,398
Once the concept is decided,
my right hand can draw anything.

286
00:16:55,398 --> 00:16:58,148
I really want to start drawing quickly!

287
00:16:59,482 --> 00:17:00,797
[Version Two, Concept Proposal]
Modern society

288
00:17:00,797 --> 00:17:02,107
is about respecting differences
with others...

289
00:17:02,107 --> 00:17:05,684
No, no, no. It's all wrong.

290
00:17:07,648 --> 00:17:11,857
This concept is that modern society,
in the name of respect...

291
00:17:11,857 --> 00:17:13,315
Wrong!

292
00:17:13,315 --> 00:17:14,400
[Version Three, Concept Proposal]
Modern society,

293
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,690
despite having more freedom...

294
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:20,788
No, no, wrong. Wrong in a different way.

295
00:17:21,732 --> 00:17:24,398
Then let me proceed with Plan B.

296
00:17:24,398 --> 00:17:25,690
Huh?

297
00:17:25,690 --> 00:17:28,232
Mr. Seo, please participate
in this competition.

298
00:17:28,232 --> 00:17:29,857
Competition?

299
00:17:29,857 --> 00:17:32,497
[Official Mascot Design: Open Call!]
It's a mascot character creation competition

300
00:17:32,497 --> 00:17:33,982
for a new shopping mall in Nerima.

301
00:17:33,982 --> 00:17:36,940
The concept has already been decided
by the client, so just draw accordingly.

302
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:39,648
No, no, no. Why do I have to do this?

303
00:17:39,648 --> 00:17:43,648
Creating a new character
takes a long time to generate profit.

304
00:17:43,648 --> 00:17:46,898
If you only do that,
Seo Design could even go bankrupt.

305
00:17:46,898 --> 00:17:48,000
Okay, that's an unnecessary worry.

306
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,920
This place is my grandma's house.

307
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:53,773
And honestly, my living expenses
are just a drop in the bucket.

308
00:17:53,773 --> 00:17:55,565
Then I'll be honest.

309
00:17:55,565 --> 00:18:00,512
Mr. Seo, your track record is too weak!

310
00:18:00,512 --> 00:18:04,815
Weak? Huh? That has nothing
to do with creating a hit!

311
00:18:04,815 --> 00:18:08,482
Yes, it does. Even if you create
a new character in the future,

312
00:18:08,482 --> 00:18:10,232
with this track record,
no one will even look at it!

313
00:18:10,232 --> 00:18:12,190
No, no. This is the Reiwa era now!

314
00:18:12,190 --> 00:18:15,565
It's an era where even unknown creators
can easily get hits from social media!

315
00:18:15,565 --> 00:18:19,456
Creators and characters who never made it
are a dime a dozen online.

316
00:18:19,456 --> 00:18:22,132
Are you really okay with being one of them?

317
00:18:22,857 --> 00:18:28,982
Man, such consultant talk is kind of scary.
I'm going to the bathroom.

318
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:33,773
Shifting responsibility because you can't
come up with a good concept is scary.

319
00:18:35,315 --> 00:18:36,512
What are you doing?
I'm going to the bathroom!

320
00:18:36,512 --> 00:18:40,000
I will take responsibility for the concept
to create a huge hit.

321
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,648
But in the meantime, you,
who are just spacing out, should...

322
00:18:44,648 --> 00:18:47,315
Who's spacing out? Even I,
despite appearances, do actually...

323
00:18:47,315 --> 00:18:49,120
If you don't draw, there won't be any hit!

324
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:55,232
Competition, competition...

325
00:18:55,232 --> 00:18:59,648
<i>♪ Making a face like a hitman ♪</i>

326
00:18:59,648 --> 00:19:04,148
<i>♪ Lunging into the competition ♪</i>

327
00:19:04,148 --> 00:19:08,648
<i>♪ Though I don't have any confidence at all ♪</i>

328
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:13,648
<i>♪ Aren't you leaving
the concept making to me? ♪</i>

329
00:19:13,648 --> 00:19:21,648
<i>♪ Because I'm a girl who messes up ♪</i>

330
00:19:23,424 --> 00:19:25,664
Concept.

331
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:32,416
Concept, concept...

332
00:19:32,416 --> 00:19:34,336
Concept.

333
00:19:34,336 --> 00:19:38,900
This is a big hit.

334
00:19:42,688 --> 00:19:44,724
Berry.

335
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,568
[Nerima Design Competition Day]
No, you know,

336
00:19:49,568 --> 00:19:51,712
my right hand is telling me that

337
00:19:51,712 --> 00:19:58,484
draw like this, and the first screening
will be a piece of cake.

338
00:20:01,824 --> 00:20:03,463
Is what you're doing really
more important than my story?

339
00:20:03,463 --> 00:20:07,636
Sorry, but I'm creating
a big hit concept right now.

340
00:20:09,056 --> 00:20:11,508
If you want, shall I listen?

341
00:20:12,288 --> 00:20:16,640
Well, roughly speaking,
why couldn't Berry become like Hello Kitty?

342
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:19,488
The law of hits learned from failure,
something like that.

343
00:20:19,488 --> 00:20:21,472
Please look forward to it.

344
00:20:21,472 --> 00:20:23,200
- What are you saying?
- No, so,

345
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:26,624
- why couldn't Berry...
- Berry, a failure? Huh?

346
00:20:26,624 --> 00:20:27,648
Huh, but actually...

347
00:20:27,648 --> 00:20:30,560
Berry isn't on that kind of stage.

348
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:33,204
Don't talk like you know
what you're saying, amateur.

349
00:20:35,289 --> 00:20:37,984
Thank you for waiting. Number three.

350
00:20:37,984 --> 00:20:39,936
- Yes.
- Right this way.

351
00:20:39,936 --> 00:20:41,684
Excuse me.

352
00:20:45,856 --> 00:20:47,356
[Merry Co., Ltd., Takaaki Hirose]

353
00:20:48,608 --> 00:20:50,164
Seo.

354
00:20:55,118 --> 00:20:56,224
Wait! Seo!

355
00:20:56,224 --> 00:20:57,248
Wait, wait!

356
00:20:57,248 --> 00:20:59,486
- Mr. Hirose, now...
- Excuse me. Well...

357
00:20:59,486 --> 00:21:00,486
No, no, no!

358
00:21:00,486 --> 00:21:02,900
Excuse me. Let me go.

359
00:21:20,608 --> 00:21:22,688
<i>Hmph, hmph, hmph.</i>

360
00:21:22,688 --> 00:21:26,149
Molco...

361
00:21:26,149 --> 00:21:30,688
Mr. Seo, Mr. Seo, Mr. Seo!

362
00:21:30,688 --> 00:21:33,632
Um, someone help! Please...

363
00:21:33,632 --> 00:21:36,008
[Emergency Entrance]
I'm truly sorry.

364
00:21:36,008 --> 00:21:39,540
Yes. All right then, please excuse me.

365
00:21:42,331 --> 00:21:44,660
Um, excuse me.

366
00:21:45,632 --> 00:21:48,211
Excuse me. I'm really sorry about that.

367
00:21:48,211 --> 00:21:51,424
No, it was my fault. I misjudged my strength.

368
00:21:51,424 --> 00:21:56,404
You just like aikido, Ms. Sasaoka.
Even though you're still a beginner.

369
00:21:58,016 --> 00:22:01,280
Let me reintroduce myself.
My surname is Hirose, I work at Merry.

370
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:04,576
Sorry, I don't have a business card.
I'll take one, thank you.

371
00:22:04,576 --> 00:22:07,936
At Seo Design, I'm not a consultant.

372
00:22:07,936 --> 00:22:10,880
I guess I kind of help out.
My surname is Kusakabe.

373
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,904
[Merry Character Producer, Suzuka Sasaoka
Merry Planner, Takaaki Hirose]

374
00:22:11,904 --> 00:22:14,080
By the way, you two and Mr. Seo...

375
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:18,176
We're colleagues.
Ah, sorry. Former colleagues.

376
00:22:18,176 --> 00:22:21,446
But you two both work at Merry, right?

377
00:22:21,446 --> 00:22:25,146
Seo was originally a designer at Merry too.

378
00:22:25,863 --> 00:22:29,963
What? He never said a word about that.

379
00:22:31,988 --> 00:22:35,136
So he actually used to do
proper character design.

380
00:22:35,136 --> 00:22:36,988
Not only that,

381
00:22:36,988 --> 00:22:41,120
Seo was the main character designer for this.

382
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:42,688
For Cynical Molco?

383
00:22:42,688 --> 00:22:45,905
- Wait, Mr. Hirose, that...
- Also, Bean Snack Mamepon,

384
00:22:45,905 --> 00:22:49,664
Dreaming Kokeko, Petal Brothers, Hara,
Hire, and Hore. He designed them all.

385
00:22:49,664 --> 00:22:51,776
Sorry, that was off the record.

386
00:22:51,776 --> 00:22:54,821
Merry has a philosophy that
characters are the protagonists,

387
00:22:54,821 --> 00:22:57,946
so we don't disclose the names
of the designers in charge.

388
00:22:57,946 --> 00:23:01,488
That's why even if you check
his background, there's nothing.

389
00:23:01,488 --> 00:23:03,071
Mr. Seo.

390
00:23:03,696 --> 00:23:05,030
Didn't you forget this?

391
00:23:05,030 --> 00:23:07,380
No, it's not mine.

392
00:23:15,552 --> 00:23:18,260
Taxi! Taxi! Taxi!

393
00:23:19,744 --> 00:23:23,155
Anywhere is fine! Just go straight for now!

394
00:23:23,155 --> 00:23:27,040
What's this? Why are you running away?

395
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,160
Wait, wait! Seo!

396
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:30,388
Quick, quick! Go!

397
00:23:38,030 --> 00:23:40,988
I see, so Mr. Seo is in the competition.

398
00:23:40,988 --> 00:23:42,336
Understood.

399
00:23:42,336 --> 00:23:43,924
[Merry President, Takumi Omishima]
Consultant?

400
00:23:44,571 --> 00:23:46,996
Her surname is Kusakabe.

401
00:23:48,608 --> 00:23:50,132
I see.

402
00:23:51,238 --> 00:23:54,580
Thank you for contacting me. Well, then.

403
00:23:56,896 --> 00:23:59,572
What's the matter?

404
00:24:00,446 --> 00:24:04,384
It's nothing. I just heard
a nostalgic name, that's all.

405
00:24:04,384 --> 00:24:06,030
It's the icing on the cake.

406
00:24:06,030 --> 00:24:07,780
It's hot, so please be careful.

407
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:12,768
So, what is it you wanted
to talk about, Ms. Mondo?

408
00:24:12,768 --> 00:24:16,084
[Merry Chief Designer, Mariko Mondo]
It's about Mizuki Seo.

409
00:24:21,856 --> 00:24:24,530
Why were you hiding it?

410
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:26,738
If you have the title of
Cynical Molco's designer...

411
00:24:26,738 --> 00:24:28,896
I hate it.

412
00:24:28,896 --> 00:24:30,155
What?

413
00:24:30,155 --> 00:24:33,446
Cynical Molco. So don't use that title.

414
00:24:33,446 --> 00:24:35,456
But you were the one who designed it, right?

415
00:24:35,456 --> 00:24:40,155
I mean, even I, with the title of
Molco's creator, could create a hit.

416
00:24:40,155 --> 00:24:45,140
But no, I asked to do it without that title.
To work hard without it.

417
00:24:46,688 --> 00:24:48,372
Mr. Seo.

418
00:24:50,144 --> 00:24:54,068
Don't you think that's a value
that only you have?

419
00:24:55,648 --> 00:24:58,484
Isn't it something that not everyone has?

420
00:24:59,552 --> 00:25:06,148
So I think we should make that
special value even bigger.

421
00:25:06,148 --> 00:25:09,152
That way, we should be able to make

422
00:25:09,152 --> 00:25:12,189
the characters that you create
into huge hits.

423
00:25:12,189 --> 00:25:13,939
So...

424
00:25:20,288 --> 00:25:22,868
You are just like those people. I knew it.

425
00:25:24,864 --> 00:25:26,816
Hey.

426
00:25:26,816 --> 00:25:29,332
Is that value really that important?

427
00:25:30,814 --> 00:25:32,731
Important to whom?

428
00:25:32,731 --> 00:25:35,689
I have my own love,
something that's important to me.

429
00:25:35,689 --> 00:25:40,189
And you're not looking at that at all.
Or rather, you can't even see it.

430
00:25:41,952 --> 00:25:45,236
It's not me who needs that value, it's you.

431
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:48,212
Driver, please stop here.

432
00:25:54,464 --> 00:25:56,820
And you can stop helping out with me, too.

433
00:26:07,552 --> 00:26:09,856
<i>Your cooking</i>

434
00:26:09,856 --> 00:26:12,731
[Kitchen Sakoda]
is a victory that only you two have.

435
00:26:12,731 --> 00:26:17,106
It's special, able to deliver the name of
Kitchen Sakoda to the world.

436
00:26:17,106 --> 00:26:21,376
If we can just rebuild the shop,
that would already be enough.

437
00:26:21,376 --> 00:26:24,948
[From a Local Western Restaurant
to a Global Brand]

438
00:26:30,273 --> 00:26:31,892
Again.

439
00:26:33,696 --> 00:26:35,284
I...

440
00:26:41,952 --> 00:26:43,552
Mr. Seo.

441
00:26:44,832 --> 00:26:47,060
It's been a while.

442
00:26:48,896 --> 00:26:51,644
Won't you come back to Merry?

443
00:26:54,048 --> 00:26:58,716
As the chief of the character design team.

444
00:26:59,856 --> 00:27:01,648
But Ms. Mondo is the chief...

445
00:27:01,648 --> 00:27:05,364
This is also Ms. Mondo's wish.

446
00:27:06,912 --> 00:27:10,868
Let's create the next hit character together.

447
00:27:13,023 --> 00:27:15,924
President, it's almost time.

448
00:27:17,568 --> 00:27:21,524
I'm looking forward to a good reply.

449
00:27:26,856 --> 00:27:29,876
[Kitchen Sakoda]

450
00:27:35,439 --> 00:27:37,814
Welcome.

451
00:27:43,264 --> 00:27:45,106
I already told you, didn't I?

452
00:27:45,106 --> 00:27:47,981
You don't have to force
yourself to come here.

453
00:27:47,981 --> 00:27:51,840
I'm not forcing myself.
I just came here because I want to eat.

454
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:53,760
Thank you for the food.

455
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:57,231
[Kitchen Sakoda Owner, Tsutomu Sakoda]

456
00:28:04,481 --> 00:28:05,814
Don't disturb.

457
00:28:05,814 --> 00:28:07,356
Disturb, disturb, disturb.

458
00:28:07,356 --> 00:28:09,556
- Disturb.
- No, I...

459
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:15,892
Lately, I've been thinking that
more and more.

460
00:28:16,512 --> 00:28:20,212
I'll handle the end of
this restaurant myself.

461
00:28:25,568 --> 00:28:30,898
When you invited me to aim for the world,

462
00:28:30,898 --> 00:28:33,314
without thinking deeply,

463
00:28:33,314 --> 00:28:40,052
I entrusted all my precious
things, things I love,

464
00:28:41,481 --> 00:28:46,484
and it was my responsibility.

465
00:28:49,939 --> 00:28:53,984
So no matter what,

466
00:28:53,984 --> 00:28:58,740
I'll handle the end of
this restaurant myself.

467
00:29:30,606 --> 00:29:32,404
[Bean Snack Mamepon]

468
00:29:37,632 --> 00:29:40,192
Did you say that Ms. Kusakabe
is back in consulting?

469
00:29:40,192 --> 00:29:43,939
Yeah, well, she said she's just helping out.

470
00:29:43,939 --> 00:29:47,398
What was it again?
Seo Design or something, right?

471
00:29:47,398 --> 00:29:49,981
Seo Design?

472
00:29:58,148 --> 00:30:00,481
Hello, this is Kusakabe
from Horai Consulting...

473
00:30:00,481 --> 00:30:03,104
No, I mean, Kusakabe. Just Kusakabe.

474
00:30:03,104 --> 00:30:05,606
<i>It's been a while. This is Fuchinobe.</i>

475
00:30:05,606 --> 00:30:08,096
Fuchinobe...

476
00:30:08,096 --> 00:30:10,356
Ah, Fuchinobe. What's up?

477
00:30:10,356 --> 00:30:14,064
Oh, nothing, I just heard that you've
made a big comeback in consulting.

478
00:30:14,064 --> 00:30:15,773
I heard through the grapevine.

479
00:30:15,773 --> 00:30:18,439
That's not true! Tell the person
who said that...

480
00:30:18,439 --> 00:30:22,773
And that your client is Seo Design.
I also heard that through the grapevine.

481
00:30:22,773 --> 00:30:27,148
It's Kominami, right? That rumor,
it's definitely Kominami!

482
00:30:27,148 --> 00:30:30,731
Seo Design. That means Mizuki Seo, right?

483
00:30:30,731 --> 00:30:32,648
The designer of Cynical Molco.

484
00:30:32,648 --> 00:30:35,273
Wait, how do you know so much?

485
00:30:35,273 --> 00:30:36,608
<i>Because I'm Fuchinobe,</i>

486
00:30:36,608 --> 00:30:40,768
the communication monster
of the consulting world.

487
00:30:40,768 --> 00:30:43,616
But more importantly,
are you really doing that?

488
00:30:43,616 --> 00:30:45,696
Consulting for Seo Design?

489
00:30:45,696 --> 00:30:49,898
No. Like I said, now it's already...

490
00:30:49,898 --> 00:30:52,981
<i>Oh, so you're not doing it.</i>

491
00:30:52,981 --> 00:30:54,981
That's good, then.

492
00:30:54,981 --> 00:30:56,576
It's just that I heard something about

493
00:30:56,576 --> 00:30:59,814
<i>Merry asking Mizuki Seo
to return to the company,</i>

494
00:30:59,814 --> 00:31:02,939
<i>and I was worried you might have
gotten caught up in something weird.</i>

495
00:31:02,939 --> 00:31:04,648
Back to Merry?

496
00:31:46,439 --> 00:31:47,956
Seo?

497
00:31:50,304 --> 00:31:51,398
What is it? What's wrong?

498
00:31:51,398 --> 00:31:53,876
Oh, nothing. It's just...

499
00:31:56,439 --> 00:31:58,981
If you don't mind, please come this way.

500
00:31:58,981 --> 00:32:02,516
You came all this way, Mr. Seo.

501
00:32:04,439 --> 00:32:07,604
If you had contacted me,
I would have come to you.

502
00:32:19,523 --> 00:32:23,956
About that talk of me coming back to Merry...

503
00:32:29,731 --> 00:32:31,572
I don't think it's possible.

504
00:32:33,606 --> 00:32:37,814
No matter how hard I try,
I just can't think of you as being right.

505
00:32:37,814 --> 00:32:41,524
So I can't create characters with you.

506
00:32:46,481 --> 00:32:52,512
No, I'm sorry. It seems
I've caused a misunderstanding.

507
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:56,704
It's not you who will
create characters, it's her.

508
00:32:56,704 --> 00:32:59,136
She's a new designer at our company.

509
00:32:59,136 --> 00:33:00,704
[Merry Character Designer, Rena Kawasaki]

510
00:33:00,704 --> 00:33:02,228
My name is Rena.

511
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:05,829
Then, that talk...

512
00:33:05,829 --> 00:33:09,204
Until now, Merry has kept
its designers' names hidden,

513
00:33:09,204 --> 00:33:11,662
but from now on,
I think we'll put them out there.

514
00:33:11,662 --> 00:33:13,376
Doing that helps us gain fans,

515
00:33:13,376 --> 00:33:15,996
which makes it easier
to sell our next creations.

516
00:33:15,996 --> 00:33:18,080
The same goes for past works.

517
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:24,832
Of course, the biggest impact
is expected from Cynical Molco's designer.

518
00:33:24,832 --> 00:33:29,780
What I want is your title.

519
00:33:30,579 --> 00:33:33,952
We'll publish the designs
she draws under your name.

520
00:33:33,952 --> 00:33:35,121
Though, of course, lying is not good.

521
00:33:35,121 --> 00:33:42,121
"The next work from the team of
Cynical Molco's designer, Mizuki Seo."

522
00:33:42,121 --> 00:33:47,860
That's the copy we plan to use.
It'll surely sell.

523
00:33:49,371 --> 00:33:54,560
So I definitely want you to come back.

524
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:56,692
Don't mess with me!

525
00:33:57,312 --> 00:33:59,252
Who would...

526
00:33:59,936 --> 00:34:02,204
I'm not joking.

527
00:34:02,204 --> 00:34:07,444
Because you don't have design talent, do you?

528
00:34:09,621 --> 00:34:13,996
You had several works that
you handled at our company, right?

529
00:34:13,996 --> 00:34:17,204
Did any one of them become a hit?

530
00:34:18,871 --> 00:34:21,287
The same goes for Molco.

531
00:34:21,287 --> 00:34:23,584
<i>With the initial settings and designs
you came up with,</i>

532
00:34:23,584 --> 00:34:24,871
<i>it didn't look happy at all.</i>

533
00:34:24,871 --> 00:34:28,288
<i>So I made some adjustments.</i>

534
00:34:28,288 --> 00:34:31,380
As a result, it became
an unprecedentedly huge hit.

535
00:34:32,412 --> 00:34:38,324
So who has the talent? You or me?

536
00:34:48,829 --> 00:34:52,621
Three years ago, you left the same way.

537
00:34:52,621 --> 00:34:55,156
I've been watching all along.

538
00:34:56,496 --> 00:35:01,684
Three years of saying
you'd prove you were right.

539
00:35:02,704 --> 00:35:05,496
And what was the result?

540
00:35:05,496 --> 00:35:10,079
<i>You kept making new characters
and posting them on social media every day.</i>

541
00:35:10,079 --> 00:35:14,868
<i>But how many people actually saw them?</i>

542
00:35:15,496 --> 00:35:21,537
And then, about six months ago,
the presentation of works stopped completely.

543
00:35:21,537 --> 00:35:22,662
Why?

544
00:35:22,662 --> 00:35:26,912
You didn't understand anymore,
did you, Mr. Seo?

545
00:35:26,912 --> 00:35:29,056
No matter what you drew,
nobody ever recognized it.

546
00:35:29,056 --> 00:35:32,896
Yet the Molco you rejected keeps selling.

547
00:35:32,896 --> 00:35:37,236
After all that confusion and wandering,
the only thing you arrived at

548
00:35:38,121 --> 00:35:43,348
is the fact that you have no talent.

549
00:35:44,537 --> 00:35:49,108
Mr. Seo, there are really only
two paths left for you now.

550
00:35:49,871 --> 00:35:53,268
Return to Merry, or...

551
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:56,532
quit design?

552
00:35:58,752 --> 00:36:00,756
Well, then.

553
00:36:23,412 --> 00:36:26,746
You have a look on your face saying,
"You didn't have to say that much."

554
00:36:26,746 --> 00:36:27,954
No, no.

555
00:36:27,954 --> 00:36:30,996
You have to crush your rivals while you can.

556
00:36:30,996 --> 00:36:35,162
Why such caution toward Mr. Seo?

557
00:36:35,162 --> 00:36:39,348
She's formidable, that Ms. Kusakabe.

558
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:55,121
- Can I?
- Cute.

559
00:36:55,121 --> 00:36:56,579
Where did you buy it?

560
00:36:56,579 --> 00:36:59,162
That's popular right now.

561
00:36:59,162 --> 00:37:01,079
- Can I touch it?
- Sure.

562
00:37:01,079 --> 00:37:03,988
- So cute.
- Really cute.

563
00:37:16,064 --> 00:37:18,356
Molco kick!

564
00:37:22,621 --> 00:37:24,224
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

565
00:37:24,224 --> 00:37:26,029
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

566
00:37:26,029 --> 00:37:28,162
Are you okay? Are you okay?

567
00:37:28,162 --> 00:37:29,536
What should I do? I'll call someone over.

568
00:37:29,536 --> 00:37:31,796
- Yeah.
- Okay.

569
00:37:33,568 --> 00:37:36,020
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

570
00:37:37,152 --> 00:37:38,676
Mr. Seo!

571
00:37:39,552 --> 00:37:41,396
I made it in.

572
00:37:46,592 --> 00:37:48,788
I'm sorry.

573
00:37:52,032 --> 00:37:56,128
Your feelings, which should be
the most important thing,

574
00:37:56,128 --> 00:37:57,908
were neglected.

575
00:37:59,488 --> 00:38:02,964
Consulting is just like that, isn't it?

576
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:06,644
No, it's just that I'm that kind of person.

577
00:38:09,792 --> 00:38:12,372
And that's also the reason
why I quit consulting.

578
00:38:15,597 --> 00:38:17,588
But it's precisely because of that

579
00:38:18,347 --> 00:38:21,972
I absolutely want to
see this project through.

580
00:38:25,088 --> 00:38:26,996
Then help me.

581
00:38:42,805 --> 00:38:45,180
I'm thinking of quitting character design.

582
00:38:45,180 --> 00:38:50,912
Even if I continue, it'll just drag on.
I think I've done enough.

583
00:38:50,912 --> 00:38:52,055
Please wait.

584
00:38:52,055 --> 00:38:55,572
What? Neglecting my feelings again?

585
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:58,740
Throw that away.

586
00:39:14,430 --> 00:39:16,448
No! Please stop!

587
00:39:16,448 --> 00:39:19,097
- Huh? Let go!
- No!

588
00:39:19,097 --> 00:39:21,055
- Let go!
- I'm not letting go!

589
00:39:21,055 --> 00:39:22,263
Why is your face like in The Shining?

590
00:39:22,263 --> 00:39:24,916
- I'm not letting go!
- Let go!

591
00:39:26,930 --> 00:39:29,805
What are you doing?

592
00:39:29,805 --> 00:39:31,805
You can't do that to them!

593
00:39:31,805 --> 00:39:33,305
You don't know anything about them, do you?

594
00:39:33,305 --> 00:39:34,868
I do know!

595
00:39:37,263 --> 00:39:41,013
This one is Bean Snack Mamepon,
and its rival is Karinto's Karin!

596
00:39:41,013 --> 00:39:44,472
This one is Dreaming Kokeko,
its special skill is oversleeping!

597
00:39:44,472 --> 00:39:46,013
Petal Brothers, Hara, Hire, Hore!

598
00:39:46,013 --> 00:39:50,048
Their catchphrase is, "Please pick us up!"

599
00:39:50,048 --> 00:39:51,680
I researched it all.

600
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:55,796
<i>Thoroughly. About all these
characters you created.</i>

601
00:39:57,056 --> 00:40:01,805
<i>The motifs and concepts are different,
but they're all kind of fluffy.</i>

602
00:40:01,805 --> 00:40:05,536
<i>And there's something
that really connects them.</i>

603
00:40:05,536 --> 00:40:07,348
<i>Mr. Seo.</i>

604
00:40:08,013 --> 00:40:14,868
I really felt that you made these characters
with care, that you love them.

605
00:40:17,847 --> 00:40:19,680
- What?
- It doesn't make sense, right?

606
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:20,864
Well, it doesn't make sense to me either.

607
00:40:20,864 --> 00:40:23,472
It doesn't make sense, but I understood.

608
00:40:23,472 --> 00:40:28,468
That you really love these characters.

609
00:40:30,656 --> 00:40:32,888
Hey, what are you even saying?

610
00:40:32,888 --> 00:40:36,788
Then do you prefer Cynical Molco?

611
00:40:38,305 --> 00:40:42,772
I somehow understand that
that's not the case.

612
00:40:48,055 --> 00:40:50,196
If you don't need them, can I have them?

613
00:40:58,176 --> 00:40:59,680
Give them back.

614
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:00,888
I don't want to.

615
00:41:00,888 --> 00:41:01,888
Give them back!

616
00:41:01,888 --> 00:41:03,008
I don't want to!

617
00:41:03,008 --> 00:41:04,638
- Give them back!
- I don't want to!

618
00:41:04,638 --> 00:41:06,612
Give them back!

619
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:18,836
I really hate all that love stuff.

620
00:41:27,763 --> 00:41:29,568
Ever since I was a kid,
I've loved cute things.

621
00:41:29,568 --> 00:41:34,019
- Gross, you're supposed to be a guy.
- <i>And because of that,</i>

622
00:41:34,019 --> 00:41:35,456
<i>I was teased.</i>

623
00:41:35,456 --> 00:41:37,263
Don't run away.

624
00:41:37,263 --> 00:41:39,988
I thought about giving up loving them,

625
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:44,788
but whenever I see cute things,
I'm immediately pulled back.

626
00:41:46,013 --> 00:41:49,568
Eventually, I wanted to
create things like this.

627
00:41:49,568 --> 00:41:53,440
I joined Merry, but nothing I made
ever became a hit.

628
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:58,164
But the one I thought would be
a hit turned out to be...

629
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:02,516
Full Tummy Molco.

630
00:42:05,096 --> 00:42:09,620
She's always full.

631
00:42:11,138 --> 00:42:14,016
She only ever says, "Full Molco".

632
00:42:14,016 --> 00:42:16,672
That's what's so good about her.

633
00:42:16,672 --> 00:42:21,388
But before I knew it, they changed
the design and stuff without permission,

634
00:42:21,388 --> 00:42:23,124
and made her cynical instead!

635
00:42:23,808 --> 00:42:28,948
For so long, I couldn't forgive that.

636
00:42:33,184 --> 00:42:34,740
So,

637
00:42:36,805 --> 00:42:39,796
I quit Merry, thinking I'd prove them wrong.

638
00:42:43,805 --> 00:42:45,908
But no one acknowledged me.

639
00:42:50,176 --> 00:42:52,884
No one understood me.

640
00:42:56,180 --> 00:42:58,356
It's painful.

641
00:42:58,971 --> 00:43:01,172
It's hard.

642
00:43:03,840 --> 00:43:05,972
Even though I want to quit already.

643
00:43:10,368 --> 00:43:12,148
Why?

644
00:43:18,816 --> 00:43:21,908
If you still want to create,
then let's create.

645
00:43:29,263 --> 00:43:31,604
Let's create together.

646
00:43:35,552 --> 00:43:39,228
It's not that simple.

647
00:43:42,638 --> 00:43:45,930
Then let's quit. Yes, quit.
Quit, everyone, resign.

648
00:43:45,930 --> 00:43:48,221
Congratulations on graduating
from character design.

649
00:43:48,221 --> 00:43:51,168
Huh? Why are you deciding that on your own?

650
00:43:51,168 --> 00:43:53,472
If it's so painful, so hard,
then why not just quit?

651
00:43:53,472 --> 00:43:55,013
There's no reason to continue, right?

652
00:43:55,013 --> 00:43:57,805
I said, it's not that simple!

653
00:43:57,805 --> 00:43:59,596
What part of it isn't simple?

654
00:43:59,596 --> 00:44:02,680
You can't think of anything
that isn't simple, can you?

655
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:05,305
Fired, fired. Once again, fired!

656
00:44:05,305 --> 00:44:07,552
We're not talking about that right now.

657
00:44:07,552 --> 00:44:11,471
Don't pretend it's complicated for yourself.

658
00:44:11,471 --> 00:44:15,846
It's the reason you can't quit.
Reason, reason, reason!

659
00:44:15,846 --> 00:44:19,552
I want to do it! I love it!

660
00:44:19,552 --> 00:44:22,180
Even though it's painful,
even though it's hard,

661
00:44:22,180 --> 00:44:26,596
I just can't stop loving it!

662
00:44:26,596 --> 00:44:28,763
Then just do it!

663
00:44:28,763 --> 00:44:29,888
You loving it that much.

664
00:44:29,888 --> 00:44:32,805
I'm already at the point
where I want to see what happens.

665
00:44:32,805 --> 00:44:36,805
In fact, I'm bursting with excitement,
totally in 'let's do this together' mode.

666
00:44:36,805 --> 00:44:40,788
I'm in 'let's make it a huge hit' mode!

667
00:44:48,888 --> 00:44:50,996
I'll do it.

668
00:44:52,288 --> 00:44:54,484
I'll do it!

669
00:44:55,712 --> 00:45:01,204
Right back at you. I'll do it too!

